  "At Google SRE autonomy level L2 (Partial), the system can monitor, investigate and actuate, but a human must explicitly approve any plan before actuation.": 1,
  "At Google SRE autonomy level L3 (High), the AI agent can detect, decide and act without human approval for bounded, well-defined scenarios, with humans often notified and safety relying heavily on technical controls and guardrails.": 1,
  "At Google SRE autonomy level L4 (Full), a system devises and executes action sequences, monitors the impact of its interventions, adapts strategy (alternative mitigations or rollbacks), and manages the incident until the system is confirmed stable.": 1,
  "Google SRE defines five AI autonomy levels (L0 Manual, L1 Assisted, L2 Partial, L3 High, L4 Full) across the functions Monitor, Investigate, Mitigate, Actuate and Self Direct.": 1,
  "Google SRE defines five AI autonomy levels: L0 Manual, L1 Assisted, L2 Partial, L3 High, and L4 Full, based on whether automation or humans handle Monitor, Investigate, Mitigate, Actuate, and Self Direct.": 1,
  "Google SRE enforces strict architectural guardrails for any AI agent interacting with production, to support what it calls the Safety Trifecta.": 1,
  "Google SRE uses Progressive Authorization: AI agents are not granted full production access from day one, are released at lower autonomy levels (human approved), and are scaled up based on the SRE Autonomy Levels.": 1,
  "Google SRE's AI-Ops governance model, the 'Safety Trifecta', consists of Transparency, Real-time Risk Evaluation, and Progressive Authorization.": 1,
