  "Google evaluates agents with datasets graded Bronze (heuristic autolabelers), Silver (programmatic, calibrated against Gold) and Gold (human-expert verified), using stratified sampling of incidents for manual review to create Gold data.": 1,
  "Google requires agent identities to be distinct from human users, strongly authenticated, and granted access only on-demand with necessary permissions (no ambient access, least privilege).": 1,
  "Google requires agent-specific rate limits and automated circuit breakers to prevent runaway loops, and requires any agent action to be highly interruptible.": 1,
  "Google requires any system or API intended for agent interaction to support a declarative dry_run=true mode so the outcome and blast radius can be predicted before production state is mutated.": 1,
